{"abstract":[{"text":"What to decide before a server is reachable by others, and what the framework does for you.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/SecurityAndLimits"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"NanoHTTP"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Security and Limits"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"NanoHTTP is made for servers inside apps and tools that are used by you, your own devices or a small trusted group.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It has ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no TLS, no authentication and no rate limiting","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". This article lists what you have to decide, and what the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"framework guards against.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"1-Who-can-connect","level":3,"text":"1. Who can connect","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By default the server accepts connections from this machine only (the loopback address ","type":"text"},{"code":"127.0.0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). A server that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"meant to be reached from other devices has to say so:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.configuration.listenAddress = .allInterfaces      // everybody who can reach this machine","try server.start(8080)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Or listen at the address of one network interface, ","type":"text"},{"code":".address(\"192.168.1.20\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"start","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" throws if the address is not an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"address of this machine, instead of listening everywhere.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Even a server that listens on the loopback address can be reached by every web page that the user opens, because the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"browser runs on the same machine. The next point matters for such servers too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"2-Which-sites-may-use-it-Host-and-Origin","level":3,"text":"2. Which sites may use it: `Host` and `Origin`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A web page can send requests to ","type":"text"},{"code":"http://localhost:8080","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (and open WebSockets to it). Two attacks use that:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"DNS rebinding:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the page’s own domain is made to point to ","type":"text"},{"code":"127.0.0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The browser then treats your server as part of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the page’s site and lets the page read every answer, with the domain of the attacker in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Host","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" header.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Requests of other sites:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" a page makes the browser send a form, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"fetch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a WebSocket handshake to your server;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the request carries the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Origin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of the page. A server that changes something when it is asked to (a ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deletes a file) does so for any page the user has open.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The server can refuse both. The checks are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"off by default","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", so that nothing changes for servers that are reached under other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names, and you switch them on in the configuration:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.configuration.hostPolicy = .automatic       // only localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1] (a server on the loopback address)","server.configuration.originPolicy = .sameOrigin    // pages of the server itself, not the pages of other sites","try server.start(8080)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/HostPolicy-swift.enum/automatic","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" accepts the names of the loopback address (","type":"text"},{"code":"localhost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"127.0.0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"[::1]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", at any port, so that a tunnel works) when the server listens only there, and every name when it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"listens at other addresses, because it cannot know the names under which it is reached. For those servers use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/HostPolicy-swift.enum/hosts(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":".hosts([\"mac.local\", \"192.168.1.20:8080\"])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; an entry without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"port accepts every port.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/OriginPolicy-swift.enum/sameOrigin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" looks at the requests that change something (everything but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"GET","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"HEAD","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"OPTIONS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and at WebSocket handshakes: when such a request has an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Origin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" header, the origin has to be the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"address that the request was sent to. Requests without an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Origin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"curl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", apps, other tools) are served, and so are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads of pages of other sites: the browser keeps those pages from reading the answer, unless you allow it with CORS (below).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/OriginPolicy-swift.enum/origins(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" adds the pages of other origins that you trust:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".origins([\"https://app.example\", \"http://localhost:3000\"])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A request that is refused is answered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"403 Forbidden","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before the middleware sees it, and logged as a warning with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the offending header. A request without a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Host","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (HTTP/1.0) is served.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The same checks exist as middleware, for the parts of a server that need other rules than the rest: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoMiddleware/hostAllowlist(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoMiddleware/originAllowlist(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sites that may use the server:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" if a page of another site is meant to talk to your server, the browser has to be told so:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"add ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoMiddleware/cors(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which answers the preflight requests of browsers and adds the headers that give the page access.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"CORS decides what a page may ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"read","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"; it does not keep the request from reaching your server, which is what the ","type":"text"},{"code":"originPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is for. List the same origins in both:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","let trusted = [\"https://app.example\", \"http://localhost:3000\"]","server.configuration.originPolicy = .origins(trusted)","server.middleware.append(NanoMiddleware.cors(NanoCORSPolicy(allowedOrigins: trusted)))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"3-Who-is-it-authentication-and-encryption","level":3,"text":"3. Who is it: authentication and encryption","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There is no TLS: everybody on the network path can read and change what is sent. For anything secret, terminate TLS","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in front of the server (a reverse proxy) or do not use the network. Authentication is yours to do, for example with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"token in a middleware as in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Compare secrets in constant time if they protect something","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"valuable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"4-Limits-on-requests","level":3,"text":"4. Limits on requests","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A single request cannot exhaust the memory of the process. Requests are limited, and requests that exceed a limit are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"answered and the connection is closed:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Limit (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser/Limits-swift.struct","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Default","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Answer","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"maxLineLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": request line, header line","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"8 KiB","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"414 URI Too Long","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" / ","type":"text"},{"code":"431","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"maxHeaderBytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": request line and all headers","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"64 KiB","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"431 Request Header Fields Too Large","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"maxBodyBytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": body (","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Length","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"64 MiB","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"413 Content Too Large","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"maxMultipartParts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": parts of a ","type":"text"},{"code":"multipart/form-data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" body","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1000","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"parseMultiPartFormData()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns no parts","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"maxMultipartHeaderBytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": headers of one part","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"16 KiB","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"parseMultiPartFormData()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns no parts","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A request that cannot be parsed (an invalid request line, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Length","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that is not a number) is answered with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"400 Bad Request","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Set the limits before starting the server; the body is held in memory, so lower the limit if you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"do not expect big uploads:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.configuration.limits = NanoHTTPParser.Limits(maxLineLength: 4 * 1024,","                                                    maxHeaderBytes: 16 * 1024,","                                                    maxBodyBytes: 1024 * 1024)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"WebSocket messages are limited by ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxMessageSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (16 MiB by default), see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/WebSockets","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"5-Time-and-the-number-of-connections","level":3,"text":"5. Time and the number of connections","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every connection occupies a thread, so connections that do nothing are limited as well","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/ThreadingAndLifecycle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"idleTimeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (60 s): a connection that sends no request is closed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"readTimeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (30 s): a request that stalls half way is answered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"408 Request Timeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"writeTimeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (30 s): a peer that does not read its response is dropped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"maxConnections","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (128): further connections are answered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"503 Service Unavailable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.configuration.idleTimeout = 15","server.configuration.maxConnections = 64"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The timeouts are pauses, not total times: a client that sends one byte every 29 seconds is not stopped, so this does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not make the server safe against slow-request attacks. What is not limited: the time a handler takes, and the rate of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For a server that strangers can reach, put a reverse proxy in front of it that provides TLS, timeouts and rate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"limits, or use another server.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"6-Output","level":3,"text":"6. Output","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The decoded ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/path","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", the query values and the values of route variables are decoded once, and can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contain anything: line breaks (","type":"text"},{"code":"%0A","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), NUL characters (","type":"text"},{"code":"%00","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"..","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Log ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/rawPath","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" instead, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never decode the values again: a check that sees ","type":"text"},{"code":"%2e%2e","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" while the use decodes it to ","type":"text"},{"code":"..","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a way out of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directory. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/ReadingRequests","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Text that is not under your control and is inserted into HTML must be escaped:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/Swift/String/htmlEscaped","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse/Body-swift.enum/htmlBody(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" inserts its content as it is. The NanoHTML","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module escapes text and attribute values itself; only ","type":"text"},{"code":"Raw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inserts HTML as it is. ","type":"text"},{"code":"browse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" escapes file names itself.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Values of response headers cannot inject headers: line breaks in them are replaced, and headers with invalid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names are dropped. Still, validate a redirect target (","type":"text"},{"code":".movedTemporarily(location)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") that comes from a request:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it may point to another site.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Files: see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/ServingFiles","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Files outside the shared directory are not served, and links that lead out of it are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refused unless you opt in.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Never use a name from a request (an upload’s file name, a route variable) as a file path without checking it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP":{"abstract":[{"text":"A small HTTP/1.1 server for apps and tools: routing, files, forms, uploads and WebSockets, without dependencies.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"NanoHTTP","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending":{"abstract":[{"text":"Look at every request before it is routed, and replace parts of the server by subclassing.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Middleware and Extending the Server","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/middlewareandextending"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser/Limits-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"text":"Upper bounds for the size of a request.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Limits"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParser/Limits-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Limits"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPParser.Limits","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpparser/limits-swift.struct"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParserError":{"abstract":[{"text":"The reasons why ","type":"text"},{"code":"NanoHTTPParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" refuses a request. A server answers requests that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fail with one of these errors with the matching HTTP status code and closes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connection; failures of the connection itself (peer closed, reset) surface as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NanoSocketError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPParserError"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPParserError","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPParserError"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPParserError","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpparsererror"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/path":{"abstract":[{"text":"The path of the request, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"decoded","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"/a%20b/%C3%A9","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"/a b/é","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"+","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stays a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"+","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"%2F","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that cannot be told from a separator any more (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/rawPath","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can). Text that is not valid percent-encoding is kept as it is, and bytes that are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not valid UTF-8 become U+FFFD.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"path"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/path","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"path","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttprequest/path"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/rawPath":{"abstract":[{"text":"The path of the request as the client sent it, still percent-encoded (","type":"text"},{"code":"/a%20b/%C3%A9","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without the query. The router matches this, one segment at a time, so that an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoded slash (","type":"text"},{"code":"%2F","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") stays inside its segment. Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/path","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to read the path; set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"rawPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (for example in middleware) to route the request to another path.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rawPath"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/rawPath","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"rawPath","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttprequest/rawpath"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse/Body-swift.enum/htmlBody(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":".html","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" body with a complete document around ","type":"text"},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"<html><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><body>content</body></html>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The content is inserted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as it is: escape text that does not come from you with ","type":"text"},{"code":"String.htmlEscaped","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"htmlBody"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A12HTTPResponseV4BodyO","text":"Body"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse/Body-swift.enum/htmlBody(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"htmlBody(_:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpresponse/body-swift.enum/htmlbody(_:)"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"text":"How a server listens and what it accepts. Change it before ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"running server keeps the configuration it was started with.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Configuration"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Configuration"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServerIO.Configuration","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/HostPolicy-swift.enum/automatic":{"abstract":[{"text":"A server that listens at the loopback address only answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"localhost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"127.0.0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"[::1]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (at any port, so that a tunnel to another port works); a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server that listens at other addresses answers every ","type":"text"},{"code":"Host","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because the names","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under which it is reached are not known.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"automatic"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/